ssion>Permissions</a></li> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#setting>Settings</a></li> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#event>Events</a></li> </ul> </div> </div> <div class=\"twelve wide column\"> <h3 id=group>Groups</h3> <p>Groups are containers that associate users with permissions. Instead of giving each individual user a set of particular permissions, we use groups to give those permissions to multiple users.</p> <h4 id=group-create>Create group</h4> <p> Superuser can create as much groups as needed. To create a group go to System -> Groups and click 'Create new group' button. Fill in group name and description and click on 'Create group' button. Make group name descriptive to indicate class of users which belongs to that group (like 'Terminal operators' for group that manages terminal). </p> <p> After a group is created, users and permissions should be added to the group. If the group is empty (without associated users and/or permissions) it can be removed from the system. </p> <h4 id=group-add-permissions>Add permissions to group</h4> <p> Permissions are added to group by clicking on 'Add permissions' button when inside a group. Select desired permission from drop list and click on 'Add' button. Repeat this action for each permission you want to add to group. Read the 'Permissions' section for more info on them. </p> <p> Each permission added to group is listed with 'x' mark, clicking on it will remove the permission from the group. </p> <h4 id=group-add-users>Add users to group</h4> <p> Adding/removing users works the same way as adding permissions. Start the action by clicking on 'Add user' button when inside a group. </p> <h3 id=user>Users</h3> <p>Create new user by visiting System -> Users and click 'Create new user' button. Fill in required fields and click on 'Create user' button. New users are not active by default, instead an email is sent with a link to a page where user will set his password. After the password is set, the user is activated and automatically logged in the system.</p> <p>If 'Superuser' option is checked, new user will act as a superuser.</p> <h3 id=permission>Permissions</h3> <p>Permissions are predefined, there is a permission for every single action in the system. They are grouped under a context which is usually a domain entity, such as 'Terminal' or 'Account'.</p> <p><strong>Note:</strong> 'Show' permissions is a default view for any entity, it includes view of entity collection with a search option to filter the collection, and a view of particular record from that collection. It is explicit if other permission from the same context are added to group, which means you don't need to include it for that case.</p> <p>Here is the list of available permissions grouped by context with their description:</p><p> <strong>Accounts</strong> <ul> <li><strong>Show:</strong> lists, search and display accounts</li> <li><strong>Update:</strong> update account - update merchant profile, available terminal services and active flag</li> <li><strong>Update limits:</strong> update account limits</li> <li><strong>Replenish stock:</strong> update account voucher stocks</li> <li><strong>Add terminal:</strong> add new terminal to account</li> <li><strong>Create:</strong> create new business account</li> <li><strong>Audit log:</strong> show update history</li> </ul> <strong>Terminals</strong> <ul> <li><strong>Show:</strong> lists, search and display terminals</li> <li><strong>Update:</strong> update terminal - update merchant profile, terminal settings and active flag</li> <li><strong>Reveal voucher:</strong> show last sold voucher's code</li> <li><strong>Audit log:</strong> show update history</li> </ul> <strong>Devices</strong> <ul> <li><strong>Show:</strong> lists, search and display devices</li> <li><strong>Attach:</strong> attach a device to terminal</li> <li><strong>Detach:</strong> remove device to terminal</li> <li><strong>Update:</strong> mark device as broken with a reason and optional comment</li> <li><strong>Audit log:</strong> show update history</li> </ul> <strong>Transactions</strong> <ul> <li><strong>Show:</strong> lists, search and display transactions</li> </ul> <strong>Services lodgments</strong> <ul> <li><strong>Show:</strong> lists, search and display services lodgments</li> </ul> <strong>Clients</strong> <ul> <li><strong>Show:</strong> lists, search and display clients</li> <li><strong>Update:</strong> update client - update client profile, client settings and active flag</li> <li><strong>Send message:</strong> send message to client</li> <li><strong>Add bank account:</strong> add current or savings remote bank account (via bridge to core bank system)</li> <li><strong>Audit log:</strong> show update history</li> </ul> <strong>Fees</strong> <ul> <li><strong>Show:</strong> lists, search and display fees</li> <li><strong>Update:</strong> update fee parameters</li> </ul> <strong>Limits</strong> <ul> <li><strong>Show:</strong> lists, search and display limits</li> <li><strong>Update:</strong> update limit parameters</li> </ul> <strong>Documents</strong> <ul> <li><strong>Show:</strong> lists, search and display documents</li> <li><strong>Update:</strong> update document status</li> </ul> <strong>Messages</strong> <ul> <li><strong>Show:</strong> lists, search and display messages</li> <li><strong>Reply:</strong> reply to messages</li> </ul> <strong>Products</strong> <ul> <li><strong>Show:</strong> lists, search and display products</li> <li><strong>Update:</strong> update product - update product info and stock quantity alert</li> <li><strong>Upload vouchers:</strong> upload vouchers file for a given product</li> </ul> <strong>Settings</strong> <ul> <li><strong>Show:</strong> lists, search and display settings</li> <li><strong>Update:</strong> update setting value</li> </ul> <strong>Pages</strong> <ul> <li><strong>Show:</strong> lists, search and display pages</li> <li><strong>Update:</strong> update page HTML</li> </ul> <strong>Events</strong> <ul> <li><strong>Show:</strong> lists, search and display events</li> </ul> </p><h3 id=setting>Settings</h3> <p>System constants can be set here, like notification emails. If setting is of type array then multiple entries should be separated by comma.</p> <h3 id=event>Events</h3> <p>Event table logs system errors and unusual behaviors. It is used mostly for troubleshooting and debug purposes.</p> <br> <button class=\"ui big basic button back-to-top\" style=\"display: none; z-index: 999; position: fixed; bottom: 2em;  right: 2em\" @click.prevent=utils.scrollToTop()> <i class=\"angle double up icon\"></i> Top of page </button> </div> </div> </div> "},function(e,t){e.exports=" <div> <h2 class=\"ui dividing header\"> User manual <div class=\"sub header\">Help for system management v1.2.0.</div> </h2> <div class=\"ui stackable grid\"> <div class=\"four wide column\"> <div class=\"ui segment\"> <strong>Contents</strong> <ul class=reset-left style=\"list-style-type: none\"> <li> <a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#general>General instructions</a> <ul> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#general-browser>Browser support</a></li> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#general-validators>Validating form data</a></li> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#general-notifications>Notifications</a></li> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#general-searching>Searching for records</a></li> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#general-relations>Record relations</a></li> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#general-filters>Filtering records by relation</a></li> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#general-session>Extending user's session</a></li> </ul> </li> <li> <a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#p-account>Personal accounts</a> <ul> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#p-account-details>Account details</a></li> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#p-account-update>Update account</a></li> </ul> </li> <li> <a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#b-account>Business accounts</a> <ul> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#b-account-create>Create new account</a></li> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#b-account-details>Account details</a></li> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#b-account-update>Update account</a></li> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#b-account-limits>Update limits</a></li> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#b-account-replenish>Replenish voucher</a></li> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#b-account-add-terminal>Add terminal</a></li> </ul> </li> <li> <a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#terminal>Terminals</a> <ul> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#terminal-details>Terminal details</a></li> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#terminal-update>Update terminal</a></li> </ul> </li> <li> <a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#device>Devices</a> <ul> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#device-remove>Removing device from terminal</a></li> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#device-assign>Assigning device to terminal</a></li> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#device-update>Update device</a></li> </ul> </li> <li> <a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#pos-transaction>POS transactions</a> <ul> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#pos-transaction-details>Transaction details</a></li> </ul> </li> <li> <a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#w-transaction>Wallet transactions</a> <ul> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#w-transaction-details>Transaction details</a></li> </ul> </li> <li> <a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#s-lodgment>Services lodgments</a> <ul> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#s-lodgment-details>Services lodgment details</a></li> </ul> </li> <li> <a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#fee>Transaction fees</a> <ul> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#fee-update>Update fee</a></li> </ul> </li> <li> <a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#limit>Transaction limits</a> <ul> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#limit-update>Update limit</a></li> </ul> </li> <li> <a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#client>Clients</a> <ul> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#client-details>Client details</a></li> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#client-update>Update client</a></li> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#client-message>Send message</a></li> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#client-document>Approve documents</a></li> </ul> </li> <li> <a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#message>Messages</a> <ul> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#message-send>Sending messages</a></li> </ul> </li> <li> <a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#document>Documents</a> <ul> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#document-update>Update document</a></li> </ul> </li> <li> <a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#operator>Operators</a> <ul> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#operator-update>Update operator</a></li> </ul> </li> <li> <a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#product>Products</a> <ul> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#product-update>Update product</a></li> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#product-upload>Upload products</a></li> </ul> </li> <li><a @click.prevent=scrollToAnchor($event) href=#page>Pages</a></li> </ul> </div> </div> <div class=\"twelve wide column\"> <h3 id=general>General instructions</h3> <p>Client application is built with reactive ES5 JavaScript framework so it can be run only in modern ES5-compliant browsers. It uses JWT tokens for authentication which means it does not use session cookies. Because of that, opening a link in a new browser tab/window will ask you to authenticate yourself. </p> <h4 id=general-browser>Browser support</h4> <p>Only ES5-compliant browsers are supported:</p> <ul> <li>IE: 9+</li> <li>Firefox: 46+</li> <li>Chrome: 29+</li> <li>Safari: 9.1+</li> <li>Opera: 38+</li> </ul> <p>We recommend latest version of Chrome browser.</p> <h4 id=general-validators>Validating form data</h4> <p>All form data is validated on server when form is submitted because each record must be in valid state before is saved to database. Upon form submit, each form input will be displayed with red border if its value is invalid and appropriate error message will be printed for such inputs. This message should give enough information to change the value to proper format and pass its validator on server. For example, if input is required and should be a number then 'must be filled' is printed if the value is not filled, and if letters are entered then 'must contain only digits' message is printed.</p> <h4 id=general-notifications>Notifications</h4> <p>There are three type of notification messages printed for certain actions to communicate positive/negative outcome or to print important information.</p> <p><strong>Error/negative</strong> notification message when something goes wrong which looks like this:</p> <div class=\"ui negative message\"> <i class=\"close icon\"></i> <div class=header> Login failed </div> <p>Check your email and/or password.</p> </div> <p><strong>Success/positive</strong> notification message when successful outcome is communicated looks like this:</p> <div class=\"ui success message\"> <i class=\"close icon\"></i> <div class=header> Have a nice day </div> <p>You are logged out.</p> </div> <p><strong>Information</strong> notification message when some extra data is need to be printed on screen looks like this:</p> <div class=\"ui info message\"> <i class=\"close icon\"></i> <div class=header> Last voucher is Chippie 10 </div> <p>Code: 001234522345</p> </div> <p>Any notification message can be dismissed by clicking on its x mark in upper right corner.</p> <h4 id=general-searching>Searching for records</h4> <p>Many record sets representing domain entities (clients, accounts, terminals ...) can be searched to find desired record(s) and/or to filter already displayed data. Search button is displayed on default entity's page if available.</p> <p>If the result set is large it will be paginated with pagination available at the bottom of the page. Each entity can be searched by their attributes, which includes full and in some cases partial match of entered value. For example, last name of client can be searched by full match or partially by entering at least 3 first letters of last name. Some records can be searched by minimum and maximum range, like amounts and dates for transactions.</p> <p>When searching through related records a list of available candidates will be presented in list to choose from. For example, when searching for business account you can enter one of its associated terminal id. It is also possible to search from other side of relation, in this example you can search for terminal entering its account number.</p> <h4 id=general-relations>Record relations</h4> <p>When displaying a single record that have relations to other records, its relations are shown under that record's title. Each relation is a link which will open related record(s).</p> <p>Relation can be singular or so called 'belongs to' relation (for example terminal belongs to single account) or plural or so called 'has many' relation (for example account has many terminals). When opening singular relation then a single related record is displayed, otherwise a collection of records are displayed for plural relation.</p> <h4 id=general-filters>Filtering records by relation</h4> <p>When browsing the system using relation links, the view will switch to related record(s) page filtering existing record set only to related records. On this new page a filter with title/name of original record (the one you begin with when clicked on relation link) is displayed with x mark.</p> <p>If you navigate to other tabs this filter is preserved, which means if you return back the filter will be there showing you only related records filtered by relation link previously clicked. To remove filter just click on x mark and the filter will be removed.</p> <p>Be careful when browsing through relation links because it will apply the relation filter on existing records which can be already filtered by search form or other relation filters which can result in empty result. In that case you need first to reset existing relation filters and/or the search form for related records.</p> <h4 id=general-session>Extending user's session</h4> <p>Session is extended after each mouse move, click or key press. If there is no activity in 15 minutes browser will auto reload and redirect to login page.</p> <h3 id=p-account>Personal accounts</h3> <p>Each client upon registration will get a default personal account with unique account number and initial balance set to zero for default currency. Client can also create new accounts when logged in.</p> <p>Personal account is used to pay bills, buy vouchers and transfer funds to other personal accounts. Money can be deposited to personal account in bank office, at merchant stores via top-up options on their terminals and transferring funds from their current/savings account (online in real time)</p> <p>Personal accounts management is under 'Accounts' tab in navigation bar. Default view is a paginated list showing account records sorted by balance in descending order.</p> <p>You can search for particular accounts by clicking on search button, if more than one account is found, initial list will be filtered showing only found records. Number of found records is shown in sub header.</p> <p>Clicking on the row will show that account's details.</p> <p>If only one record is found (if searching for account number for example) it will automatically show it's details. This is general behavior when using search for any entity - if a single record is found it will be shown immediately.</p> <h4 id=p-account-details>Account details</h4> <p>Details page displays account information:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Account number</strong> - shown in header</li> <li><strong>Active flag</strong> - badge shown in header</li> <li><strong>Account type</strong> - badge shown in header</li> <li><strong>Title</strong> - shown in sub header, this is set by client</li> <li><strong>Time of last update</strong> - shown in sub header</li> <li><strong>Associated records with links</strong> - transactions and clients for this account</li> <li><strong>Balance and transactions statistics</strong> - shown in main area</li> </ul> <p>At bottom of the page are the action buttons:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Edit</strong> - for updating account data</li> <li><strong>Audit log</strong> - lists last ten changes for account</li> <li><strong>Close</strong> - return to accounts list page</li> </ul> <h4 id=p-account-update>Update account</h4> <p>When updating personal account only 'active' flag can be set. If account is deactivated, all client's actions are disabled for this account. Transfers to this account are also disabled.</p> <h3 id=b-account>Business accounts</h3> <p>Business account belongs to merchant who operates one or more terminals. Business account is a container for its terminals, each terminal share data settings from parent account - merchant profile, limits, activated services and voucher stocks.</p> <p>Default view is similar to personal accounts view, it differs by data specific to business accounts. Accounts can be searched like personal accounts but more search options are available.</p> <h4 id=b-account-create>Create new account</h4> <p>To create new account click on 'Create new business account' button</p> <p>Fill in merchant's profile and account settings then click on 'Create account'. All entered data will be validated on server upon submit (email field for example must be in proper format), if all is right new account will be created.</p> <p>Only activated services will be available on this account's terminals. If account is deactivated, all terminals for this account will be blocked.</p> <h4 id=b-account-details>Account details</h4> <p>Clicking on account's row will open it's details page:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Account number</strong> - shown in header</li> <li><strong>Active flag</strong> - badge shown in header</li> <li><strong>Account type</strong> - badge shown in header</li> <li><strong>Title</strong> - shown in sub header, this is set by client</li> <li><strong>Time of last update</strong> - shown in sub header</li> <li><strong>Associated records with links</strong> - transactions, clients ant terminals for this account</li> <li><strong>Credit limit, exposure, sales amount and count</strong> - shown in main area</li> <li><strong>Merchant profile</strong> - shown in main area</li> <li><strong>Merchant settings</strong> - shown in main area</li> <li><strong>Activated services</strong> - shown in main area</li> <li><strong>Voucher stock</strong> - shown in main area</li> </ul> <p>At bottom of the page are the action buttons:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Edit</strong> - for updating account data</li> <li><strong>Update limits</strong> - for updating limits for account's terminals</li> <li><strong>Replenish voucher stock</strong> - for updating voucher stock</li> <li><strong>Add terminal</strong> - to add new terminal to account</li> <li><strong>Audit log</strong> - lists last ten changes for account</li> <li><strong>Close</strong> - return to accounts list page</li> </ul> <h4 id=b-account-update>Update account</h4> <p>Merchant's profile and account settings are updated here. You can activate/deactivate terminal services or activate/deactivate account. If account is deactivated, all terminals for this account will be blocked.</p> <h4 id=b-account-limits>Update limits</h4> <p>Merchant's exposure amount, credit limit, transaction min. amount and transaction max. amount are updated here. Input fields will automatically format numbers as currency (i.e. 1234567 will become 1,2345.67).</p> <h4 id=b-account-replenish>Replenish voucher</h4> <p>Stock is incremented by a given number for any voucher type here. Select the voucher name and enter quantity to be added to existing stock.</p> <h4 id=b-account-add-terminal>Add terminal</h4> <p>New terminal can be added to account by filling the form with required parameters.</p> <p>Merchant name, address, phone, email and contact are copied from its account. You can change any of this information if needed. This is convenience if merchant has more terminals on different locations. Receipt text is the text printed on terminal receipts (up to four lines are allowed). If terminal is deactivated all actions on the device are blocked.</p> <p>Working time uses 24 hours clock. Set values for opening and closing times from the list or check 24/7 option if the terminal will work 0-24 during the whole week.</p> <p> Enter a serial number that exist on the devices list which has status of 'Idle'. If the entered serial doesn’t exist on devices list or if its device has status of 'Failure' or 'Assigned' then the value will be marked as invalid input.</p> <p>You also need to enter full name for initial Cashier manager when creating terminal. Later on client who owns this business account can add more cashiers via web or using this cashier manager account can add more cashiers via terminal device.</p> <p>Click on 'Add terminal' button to submit form data, server will validate it and if all is right new terminal record for account is created. API key and initial PIN for default cashier is printed on screen.</p> <p><strong>NOTE:</strong> Write down the cashier PIN returned from the server upon successful creation of terminal. PIN should be delivered to terminal cashier/manager in secure way. Once the manager cashier get this pin he should change it.</p> <h3 id=terminal>Terminals</h3> <p>Terminal hold the configuration data of the physical device. Each terminal entry has its device attached using device's serial number.</p> <p>Terminals management is under 'Terminals' tab in navigation bar. Default view is a paginated list showing terminals records sorted by current batch amount (amount that is pending for settlement) in descending order.</p> <p>You can search for particular terminals by clicking on search button, if more than one terminal is found, initial list will be filtered showing only found records. Number of found records is shown in sub header.</p> <p>Clicking on the row will show that terminal's details.</p> <h4 id=terminal-details>Terminal details</h4> <p>Details page displays terminal information:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Terminal ID with merchant name</strong> - shown in header</li> <li><strong>Active flag</strong> - badge shown in header</li> <li><strong>Time of last update</strong> - shown in sub header</li> <li><strong>Associated records with links</strong> - this terminal's transactions, account and lodgments</li> <li><strong>Credit limit, exposure, sales amount and count from account</strong> - shown in main area</li> <li><strong>Merchant profile</strong> - shown in main area</li> <li><strong>Limits from terminal's account</strong> - shown in main area</li> <li><strong>Activated services from terminal's account</strong> - shown in main area</li> <li><strong>Terminal settings</strong> - shown in main area</li> <li><strong>Cashiers</strong> - shown in main area</li> </ul> <p>At bottom of the page are the action buttons:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Edit</strong> - for updating account data</li> <li><strong>Reveal last voucher</strong> - will display the value of latest sold voucher</li> <li><strong>Audit log</strong> - lists last ten changes for account</li> <li><strong>Close</strong> - return to terminals list page</li> </ul> <h4 id=terminal-update>Update terminal</h4> <p>Merchant name, address, phone, email and contact can be updated here if those differs from its account's merchant profile. This is convenience if merchant has more terminals on different locations.</p> <p>Working time uses 24 hours clock. Set values as whole numbers without leading zeros.</p> <p>Receipt text is the text printed on terminal receipts (up to four lines are allowed). If terminal is deactivated all actions on the device are blocked.</p> <h3 id=device>Devices</h3> <p>Device represents a physical POS device, it is attached to a terminal entry.</p> <p>Device management is under More -> Devices tab in navigation bar. It is also accessible from the terminal list. Default view is a paginated list showing devices records with their terminal ID, serial number and status flag.</p> <h4 id=device-remove>Removing device from terminal</h4> <p> Search for device using 'Terminal ID' or 'Serial number' (search will work also for partial serial number). Click on 'Detach from terminal' button and confirm it to remove device from the terminal. Device is now flagged as 'Idle' with the time when it was removed. </p> <h4 id=device-assign>Assigning device to terminal</h4> <p> Search for any idle device by status filter and/or its serial number. Click on 'Attach to terminal' button, enter 'Terminal ID' that has no attached device and submit the form. Device is now flagged as 'Assigned' with the time when it was assigned. This action will fail for invalid 'Terminal ID' or if terminal has already attached device. </p> <h4 id=device-update>Update device</h4> <p> If device is in status 'Idle' then it can be edited and marked as 'Failure' with failure reason and optional comment. If its in status 'Failure' it can be again set to 'Idle' which means it can be used again, </p> <h3 id=pos-transaction>POS transactions</h3> <p>POS transactions are under 'Transactions' tab in navigation bar. Default view is a paginated list showing transactions records sorted by their ID in descending order. Debit amounts are shown in red color and credit amounts are in orange color for convenience. Voided amounts are shown with strikeout text like <span class=\"striked green\">22.00 USD</span>.</p> <p>You can search for particular transactions by clicking on search button, if more than one transaction is found, initial list will be filtered showing only found records. Number of found records is shown in sub header.</p> <p>Clicking on the row will show that transaction's details.</p> <h4 id=pos-transaction-details>Transaction details</h4> <p>Details page displays transaction information:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Transaction ID</strong> - shown in header</li> <li><strong>Transaction type/credit/debit</strong> - badge shown in header</li> <li><strong>Transaction status</strong> - approved or declined</li> <li><strong>Voided</strong> - badge shown in header if its voided</li> <li><strong>Time of transaction</strong> - shown in sub header</li> <li><strong>Associated records with links</strong> - this transaction's terminal and account</li> <li><strong>List of transaction attributes</strong> - shown in main area</li> </ul> <p>Transaction attributes:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Transaction ID</strong> - unique ID for transaction</li> <li><strong>Amount with currency</strong> - deposits are in green, voids are in red</li> <li><strong>Transaction type</strong> - voucher, bill, top up, sale</li> <li><strong>Payment method</strong> - cash, card, check</li> <li><strong>Payment type</strong> - credit, debit for card method; bank name for check method</li> <li><strong>Description</strong> - name of the voucher sold or name of operator for bill payment</li> <li><strong>Note</strong> - current batch balance and customer balance for bill payment</li> <li><strong>Systan</strong> - unique identifier for batch</li> <li><strong>Reference number</strong> - for card authorization</li> <li><strong>Cashier</strong> - cashier who did the transaction</li> <li><strong>Status</strong> - approved or declined</li> </ul> <p>At bottom of the page are the action buttons to print this transaction and button to return to transactions list page.</p> <h3 id=w-transaction>Wallet transactions</h3> <p>Wallet transactions are under 'Transactions' tab in navigation bar. Default view is a paginated list showing transactions records sorted by their ID in descending order. Debit amounts are shown in red color and credit amounts are in orange color for convenience.</p> <p>You can search for particular transactions by clicking on search button, if more than one transaction is found, initial list will be filtered showing only found records. Number of found records is shown in sub header.</p> <p>Clicking on the row will show that transaction's details.</p> <h4 id=w-transaction-details>Transaction details</h4> <p>Details page displays transaction information:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Transaction ID</strong> - shown in header</li> <li><strong>Transaction type/credit/debit</strong> - badge shown in header</li> <li><strong>Transaction status</strong> - approved or declined</li> <li><strong>Time of transaction</strong> - shown in sub header</li> <li><strong>Associated records with links</strong> - this transaction's account</li> <li><strong>List of transaction attributes</strong> - shown in main area</li> </ul> <p>Transaction attributes:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Transaction ID</strong> - unique ID for transaction</li> <li><strong>Amount with currency</strong> - credits are in green, debits are in red</li> <li><strong>Transaction type</strong> - transfer, voucher, bill</li> <li><strong>Description</strong> - name of the voucher sold, name of operator for bill payment or transfer info</li> <li><strong>Note</strong> - voucher code or customer balance</li> <li><strong>Status</strong> - approved or declined</li> </ul> <p>At bottom of the page are the action buttons to print this transaction and button to return to transactions list page.</p> <h3 id=s-lodgment>Services lodgments</h3> <p>Service lodgments can be found under 'Lodgments' tab.</p> <p>Default view is a paginated list showing lodgments records in chronological order.</p> <p>You can search for particular lodgments by clicking on search button, initial list will be filtered showing only found records. Number of found records is shown in sub header.</p> <p>Click on the table row to show lodgment details.</p> <h4 id=s-lodgment-details>Services lodgment details</h4> <p>Details page displays lodgment information:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Terminal ID</strong> - shown in header</li> <li><strong>Merchant name</strong> - shown in sub header</li> <li><strong>Lodgment number</strong> - shown in sub header</li> <li><strong>Start and end time</strong> - shown in sub header</li> <li><strong>Associated records with links</strong> - this lodgment's account, terminal and transactions</li> <li><strong>Totals</strong> - shown in main area</li> <li><strong>Action buttons to show different traffic breakdowns</strong> - shown in main area</li> <li><strong>Bill payments totals</strong> - shown in main area</li> <li><strong>Voucher payments totals</strong> - shown in main area</li> </ul> <h3 id=client>Clients</h3> <p>Clients are people who register on wallet portal. Each client will get default personal account upon registration and their client type is set to 'Basic'.</p> <p>Clients can upload their documents (like passport or bill receipt) to upgrade themselves to 'Standard' type and they can also apply for a business account.</p> <p>Client type determines account traffic limits - upgraded client can do transactions more often with higher amounts.</p> <p>Clients management is under 'Clients' tab in navigation bar.</p> <p>Default view is a paginated list showing clients records sorted by registration time in descending order.</p> <p>You can search for particular clients by clicking on search button, if more than one client is found, initial list will be filtered showing only found records. Number of found records is shown in sub header.</p> <p>Clicking on the row will show that client's details.</p> <h4 id=client-details>Client details</h4> <p>Details page displays client information:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Full name</strong> - shown in header</li> <li><strong>Active flag</strong> - badge shown in header</li> <li><strong>Client type</strong> - badge shown in header</li> <li><strong>Time of last login</strong> - shown in sub header</li> <li><strong>Time of last update</strong> - shown in sub header</li> <li><strong>Associated records with links</strong> - this clients's wallet transactions and his accounts</li> <li><strong>Profile</strong> - shown in main area</li> <li><strong>Uploaded documents</strong> - shown in main area</li> </ul> <p>At bottom of the page are the action buttons:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Send message</strong> - for sending message to client using built-in messaging system</li> <li><strong>Edit</strong> - for updating client profile</li> <li><strong>Audit log</strong> - lists last ten changes for client</li> <li><strong>Close</strong> - return to clients list page</li> </ul> <h4 id=client-update>Update client</h4> <p>Profile data and client type is updated here. If client is deactivated he can't log in until activated again.</p> <h4 id=client-message>Send message</h4> <p>Operator can send messages to clients and client can reply to those messages. Use this for internal communications with clients. Read more about sending and receiving messages under 'Messages' section.</p> <h4 id=client-document>Approve documents</h4> <p>Clients will upload their documents for identity verification (passport, utility bill and such). Each document can be approved or rejected with a note to client why the document is rejected (poor scan or too old document for example). When certain document is approved client can be promoted from 'Basic' to 'Standard' type using edit form.</p> <p>Click on document title to open the document. Here you can click on 'Approve' or 'Reject' buttons if document is valid or not. For invalid documents write a note to client why the document was rejected.</p> <h3 id=fee>Transaction fees</h3> <p>Transaction fees management is under More -> Fees tab.</p> <p>There is a fee setting for each transaction type, and each fee can be applied for different account and client types. All available fees are inactive by default.</p> <p>After a transaction is generated and if its type, its account and/or client type matches a fee record, that fee will be applied on that transaction and transaction fee record will be generated with reference to the original transaction.</p> <h4 id=fee-update>Update fee</h4> <p>To update fee settings click on its row. Here you can change fee amount that will be applied to certain class of transactions.</p> <h3 id=limit>Transaction limits</h3> <p>Transaction limits management is under More -> Limits tab.</p> <p>There is a limit setting for each transaction type, and each limit can be applied for different account and client types. All available limits are inactive by default.</p> <p>When a transaction is initiated, if it matches its limit criteria it will be blocked.</p> <h4 id=limit-update>Update limit</h4> <p>To update limit settings click on its row. Here you can change amount limit that will stop processing certain class of transactions when that limit is reached.</p> <h3 id=message>Messages</h3> <p>Messages are under More -> Messages tab. Sent and received messages are grouped under 'Inbox' and 'Outbox' tabs.</p> <p>System users can communicate with clients using built-in messaging system. This can be used by support staff to help clients with the system or to send some important notifications.</p> <p>Each new message is marked as unread until receiver clicks on it so operator will now if client has read sent messages.</p> <p>Clients are not able to initiate conversation, they can only reply to messages from operator.</p> <h4 id=message-send>Sending messages</h4> <p>Message can be sent using 'Send message' button from client's profile page. When browsing messages 'Send new message' button works in similar way but it will first prompt you for a client - enter few first letters of client's last name to get list of clients and select one. Fill in subject and message fields then hit 'Send message' button. The message sent is placed in 'Outbox' tab, when client replies, it can be found in 'Inbox' tab.</p> <h3 id=document>Documents</h3> <p>It is under More -> Documents tab. Default filter for document list is by 'Pending' state. Reset search form or set another filter to list other documents.</p> <p>Clients will upload their documents for identity verification (passport, utility bill and such). Each document can be approved or rejected with a note to client why the document is rejected (poor scan or too old document for example). When certain document is approved client can be promoted from 'Basic' to 'Standard' type using edit form.</p> <h4 id=document-update>Update document</h4> <p>Click on document title to open the document. Here you can click on 'Approve' or 'Reject' buttons if document is valid or not. For invalid documents write a note to client why the document was rejected. If the document is approved, a new window is opened where client's account type can be upgraded if needed.</p> <h3 id=operator>Operators</h3> <p>It is under More -> Operators tab.</p> <p>All available operators are listed in alphabetical order and are grouped under three categories - bill, voucher and prepaid.</p> <h4 id=operator-update>Update operator</h4> <p>To update operator click on its row.</p> <p>For each operator info string can be set, it is the text that is printed on terminal receipt (up to four lines, each line can be 22 characters long due to terminal paper format). If the active flag is not set transaction processing for operator will be disabled globally (for terminals, web and mobile).</p> <h3 id=product>Products</h3> <p>It is under More -> Products tab.</p> <p>All available products are listed in alphabetical order. Click on row entry to open its details page.</p> <p>Details page displays product type (like voucher), its price and currency, its stock quantity and notification quantity. Notification quantity is an integer value used to send out emails to staff when stock quantity reaches this amount (these email addresses can be set under 'Settings' tab). Total number of sold vouchers is also shown.</p> <h4 id=product-update>Update product</h4> <p>To update operator on 'Edit' button.</p> <p>If info string for a product is set (default is empty string), it will override info string from its parent operator. Use this if you need to print on terminal receipt some specifics for a particular product.</p> <h4 id=product-upload>Upload products</h4> <p>Each product can be replenished using 'Upload products' button. Select a product from list and upload a file for that product - after upload is finished newly created products will be added to stock quantity and number of imported products is printed on the screen. If there was an error during the import (if file format is invalid for example), partially imported products are rollbacked and the error will be printed on the screen.</p> <h3 id=page>Pages</h3> <p>It is under More -> Pages tab.</p> <p>Each public facing page (about, terms ...) can be edited using HTML editor. Update pages to be up to date with bank policy.</p> <p>To update page click on its row.</p> <br> <button class=\"ui big basic button back-to-top\" style=\"display: none; z-index: 999; position: fixed; bottom: 2em;  right: 2em\" @click=utils.scrollToTop()> <i class=\"angle double up icon\"></i> Top of page </button> </div> </div> </div> ";
